  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1222 AM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nAs expected conditions are sharply cooler tonight across the\nquad-state. Moderate northwest winds should continue overnight\nwith temperatures falling into the 40s area-wide. A 1040mb\nsurface ridge sits over the western Plains with plans of sitting\novertop of this region tonight. With plenty of drier air being\npushed in with this ridge, idealized radiational cooling\nconditions amid deep layer ridging, and calm winds under the \nridge axis very strong radiational cooling conditions are \nexpected. Frost still looks likely enough area-wide to go with \nan advisory. Some areas particularly in the northern half of the\nregion could very well drop to freezing as things bottom out.\n\nGood model consensus that the upper level pattern gets blocked\nup for several days as we head into the new work week. With\nridging over the plains leading to surface ridging focused just\neast of the area. Dry conditions with low humidity and \nseasonable temperatures look likely for several days amid a\nstable/settled pattern. Highs in the low to mid 70s and lows in\nthe mid to upper 40s are projected, which is right in line with\nseasonal norms.\n\nA few Pacific troughs will take a shot at dislodging the ridging\nthrough the end of the week, but in most all guidance they are\nunsuccessful and sail well to the north of the region keeping \nthe pattern in place.",
